  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...An active weather pattern is likely from late on Thanksgiving\ninto next weekend. Forecast confidence on any particular weather\nsystem is low, but travelers should continue to monitor this \nperiod for potential travel disruptions.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nThe general weather pattern from Thanksgiving through the weekend is \nfavorable for active weather. This will likely impact holiday \ntravel. \n\nUpr low currently diving over the Canadian Rockies will deepen as it \ndigs into the upr Midwest. At the same time the s/wv near the four-\ncorners region will be ejecting into the srn Plains. Uncertainty \ncontinues to be focused on timing of pcpn moving in and how quickly \na secondary lopres can form near the waters. \n\n00z GFS is keeping both features separate from each other as it \ntraverses the central Plains whereas the EC seems to phase things \nmuch quicker with CMC being in between these soln. This is likely \nthe driver on determining how quickly pcpn moves into our CWA toward \nthe end of the week. Gut feeling and based on overall biases, GFS \ntends to move pcpn in too quickly with high pressure located to our \nnorth and east due to saturating the atmosphere too quickly. Gut \nfeeling is to side toward more of the latest CMC. This soln holds \nbulk of the pcpn off until just after 06z Fri. \n\nAs far as ptypes, this also depends on how quickly pcpn moves in. H8 \ntemps will be well above frzg at onset of pcpn though sfc temps will \nbe hovering right around the freezing mark. Cannot rule out cold air \ndamming setting up over favored areas from the Houlton area back \ntoward the Central Highlands late Thursday night and Friday morning. \nCannot rule out a brief period of fzra at onset, if onset can occur \nbefore sunrise. However, if pcpn can hold off until after 12z, this \nshould allow air temps to rise above freezing over central areas. \nThat being said, road temps may still be below freezing especially \nbridges. \n\nAdditional chances for wintry mix/ snow showers are possible through \nthe weekend, though confidence is low at this time. In summary, it \nis still early, but be aware of the potential for active weather \nthat could impact travel Thanksgiving evening through the weekend. \nContinue to check back for updates.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Noticeably colder today with gusty northwest \nwinds.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nGusty northwest winds will continue today, bringing cold\ntemperatures to the region. Temperatures this morning will be\nbelow freezing for the entire area, except for a few coastal\nspots. Temperatures will only warm up into the low 40s in the\ncoastal Downeast region, and low 30s in the North Woods. Northwest\nwinds will gust up to 25 to 30 mph today producing even colder \napparent temperatures. Apparent temperatures will range from the\nmid teens to lower 20s north, to the mid 20s to lower 30s \nDowneast. Low temperatures overnight will fall into the upper\nteens and low 20s for much of the area, except for the immediate\ncoast. Winds will diminish overnight into Wednesday. Wednesday \nwill again be cold with similar highs and lows as today \n(Tuesday).",
